error[E0277]: `u8` cannot be decrypted from one `Ciphertext`
  --> tests/ui/owned_collection_elements.rs:15:13
   |
15 |     let _ = Vec::<u8>::decrypt_from(column, keyset);
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ one `Ciphertext` decrypts into one owned value
   |
   = help: the trait `OpaqueDecode` is not implemented for `u8`
   = note: one value is a `String`, a `bool`, a float, a `Vec<u8>`, or a fixed-width integer other than `u8`. An `Option` or a `Protected` of one of these is one value too. So is a newtype that derives `Decrypt` over one of these.
   = note: the type must also implement `Zeroize`, so that a decrypted value can be wiped when a later decrypt in the same call fails.
   = note: the type must also be `Send` and `'static`. A type that borrows data is not `'static`.
   = note: to decrypt a `Vec<Ciphertext>` into a `Vec`, with one element from each `Ciphertext`, use `DecryptFrom`.
   = note: to decrypt a sequence, a map, or a struct that derives `Decrypt`, use `keyset.decrypt_tree`. `keyset.encrypt_tree` makes the tree of ciphertexts that it reads.
   = note: to decrypt a whole `Deserialize` value from one `Ciphertext`, decrypt into `OpaqueBlob<T>`. `T` must also implement `Default` and `Zeroize`.
help: the trait `OpaqueDecode` is implemented for `OpaqueBlob<T>`
  --> src/blob.rs
   |
   | impl<T: DeserializeOwned + Default + Zeroize + Send + 'static> OpaqueDecode for OpaqueBlob<T> {}
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: required for `stack_encrypt::Ciphertext` to implement `DecryptSource<u8>`
   = note: 1 redundant requirement hidden
   = note: required for `Vec<stack_encrypt::Ciphertext>` to implement `DecryptSource<Vec<u8>>`
